  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Resilience and Inclusive Trade</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TradeMark Africa&apos;s Resilience and Inclusive Trade Portfolio works from the conviction that trade facilitation only delivers on its poverty-reduction potential when it explicitly addresses the barriers faced by those most at risk of being left behind i.e. women, youth, persons with disabilities, and small-scale cross-border traders. The Portfolio operates across four interconnected areas: making regional food trade in staple crops more efficient, competitive, and climate-adaptive through improved standards compliance, storage and aggregation infrastructure, and access to finance; accelerating the movement of food aid-related cargo through green channels at One Stop Border Posts to reduce humanitarian supply chain bottlenecks; promoting trade reforms that remove specific barriers for small businesses &#x2014; including Simplified Trade Regimes, Joint Border Committees, and streamlined border processes &#x2014; while equipping traders with information, business development support, and formalisation pathways; and directly supporting women and youth to organise into cooperatives and access markets.</narrative>
  </description>
